.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::BoundaryStressVisitor< dim >"\fBBoundaryStressVisitor\fP accesses a \fBBoundary\fP object that must be a surface, computing nodal forces based on the normal and shear stresses applied to that \fBBoundary\fP element\&. If the boundary is inclined or vertical and body forces are enabled, the visitor takes the vertical variation in the boundary normal stress into account\&. 


.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
this visitor assumes that the driving stresses are Andersonian, i\&.e\&. that one of the principal stress axes is aligned with the vertical (Y)-axis of the model\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
This visitor allows for a workaround for applying stress boundary conditions if one does not want to use the Neumann condition functionality of the \fBPDE_Integrator\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Input are the \fBFace\fP variables 'normal stress' and 'shear stress\&.' The nodal forces are computed from these\&.

.PP
Use this, for instance to compute and apply overburden stresses\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
by default all forces that were previously assigned are zeroed first\&.

.PP
compressive (inward pointing) stresses are positive\&.

.PP
this visitor assumes that the far-field stress regime is Andersonian, i\&.e\&. one of the principal stresses is oriented perpendicular to the earth surface\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
SKM 29/9/2014 
.RE
.PP

